# Everything the image does not need — mostly so the 87 MB model is the only large
# thing that travels, and so no test environment, venv or local database leaks in.

# Python noise
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/

# The virtualenv is rebuilt from requirements.txt inside the image.
backend/venv/

# Test-only: the suite and its browser stack never run on the host.
backend/tests/
backend/requirements-dev.txt

# ``backend/requirements-optional.txt`` DOES travel, and that is a decision rather than an
# oversight. Each entry in it is a feature that degrades gracefully when the package is
# missing - which is why the file is not ``requirements.txt`` - but "degrades" is not "works":
# without ``pywebpush`` the deployment cannot reach a worker whose app is closed, and its own
# self-test says so (``worker_push_delivery``). The image therefore installs the extras it
# wants (see the Dockerfile); what stays out of the build context is the test stack above.

# Local state and biometric data — never in an image layer.
times.db
times.db-wal
times.db-shm
*.db.bak
backend/certs/
worker_photos/
local_references/
punch_frames/
quick_link_photos/
calibration_corpus/
temp/
backups/

# Development machinery
.freebuff/
.vscode/
.git/
docs/
deploy/cloudflare/__pycache__/

# One-off scratch files from the checkout, not the application.
*.bak
test_odoo.py

# NOT the entrypoint - it is COPYied in the Dockerfile and must travel with the image.
!docker-entrypoint.sh
